From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: skip the host ready doorbell at init once it is a capability

Since the host capabilities are written, brcmfmac enables host ready
when the firmware reports BRCMF_PCIE_SHARED_HOSTRDY_DB1, and still rings
the host ready doorbell in brcmf_pcie_preinit(). The BCM4364B3 firmware
of the MacBookPro16,1 halts on that doorbell before it answers the first
ioctl, and the BCM4364B2 firmware of the MacBookPro15,1 does so on some
loads:

  brcmf_pcie_handle_mb_data D2H_MB_DATA: FW HALT
  brcmf_attach: dongle is not responding: err=-5

Without the host ready capability the BCM4377 firmware leaves the first
ioctl unanswered, so the capability stays. With host ready enabled the
firmware takes the doorbell as the exit from D3, which is where Broadcom's
DHD driver rings it, after D0_INFORM. Ring it at init only when host ready
is not a capability. brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3() keeps ringing it after
D0_INFORM.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -326,6 +326,7 @@ struct brcmf_pcie_shared_info {
 	dma_addr_t ringupd_dmahandle;
 	u8 version;
 	bool mb_via_ctl;
+	bool hostrdy;
 };
 
 #define BRCMF_OTP_MAX_PARAM_LEN 16
@@ -1600,7 +1601,13 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_preinit(struct device *dev)
 	brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "Enter\n");
 
 	brcmf_pcie_intr_enable(buspub->devinfo);
-	brcmf_pcie_hostready(buspub->devinfo);
+	/*
+	 * Once the host capabilities enable host ready, the firmware takes the
+	 * doorbell as the exit from D3 only. The BCM4364 firmware halts on it
+	 * here.
+	 */
+	if (!buspub->devinfo->shared.hostrdy)
+		brcmf_pcie_hostready(buspub->devinfo);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1807,8 +1814,10 @@ brcmf_pcie_init_share_ram_info(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo,
 			!(shared->flags & BRCMF_PCIE_SHARED_USE_MAILBOX);
 
 		host_cap = shared->version;
-		if (shared->flags & BRCMF_PCIE_SHARED_HOSTRDY_DB1)
+		if (shared->flags & BRCMF_PCIE_SHARED_HOSTRDY_DB1) {
 			host_cap |= BRCMF_HOSTCAP_H2D_ENABLE_HOSTRDY;
+			shared->hostrdy = true;
+		}
 		if (shared->flags & BRCMF_PCIE_SHARED_DAR)
 			host_cap |= BRCMF_HOSTCAP_H2D_DAR;
 		host_cap |= BRCMF_HOSTCAP_DS_NO_OOB_DW;
